WEBVTT

00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:02.600
Thank you.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:15.200
Uh-huh.

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:37.490
Draw that car from the front. I was the way behind.

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:57.910
The soldiers of high up, bombers, pronto! The anchors will talk!

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:01.030
Get on.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:32.980
I can't.

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:42.100
This trail have been used but yesterday.

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:46.700
Wonder where it is leased, underlay.

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:47.560
- Yeah, you don't need to stay around out there any longer.

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:49.750
The old claim's petered out, Ruby.

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:51.730
I reckon we better head for town.

00:05:51.730 --> 00:05:53.420
- Well, that suits me, all right.

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:54.860
How would you like me to make you some lunch?

00:05:54.860 --> 00:05:56.640
- And am I hungry?

00:05:56.640 --> 00:06:00.000
Say, I could eat a whole can of beans, including

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.210
Hold me ten.

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:21.890
Watch out there.

00:06:21.890 --> 00:06:22.850
We may need this place.

00:06:22.850 --> 00:06:24.070
Stay here.

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:51.230
- I hope I do not intrude. - Now listen, I don't talk no flowery language,

00:06:51.230 --> 00:06:53.280
and I'm too tired to make any bows.

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:55.480
Well, let's get right to the point.

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:57.740
Who are you, and what do you want?

00:06:57.740 --> 00:07:00.000
You amuse me greatly, sir.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.420
I am come but to beg permission to water my hours.

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:05.270
You see, I am your neighbor.

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:08.360
- Neighbor? - Yes, senor.

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:10.380
I live but a few miles beyond you.

00:07:10.470 --> 00:07:12.530
My name is Don Yorva.

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:17.090
I didn't refuse anybody any water, so help yourself.

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:18.770
You are very kind, senor.

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:25.000
- Do you live here alone? - Sometimes.

00:07:34.030 --> 00:07:38.020
- This is our neighbor, Don Yorba, Ruby.

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:42.930
- How do you do, Mr. Yorba?

00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:48.460
- This is an unexpected pleasure, senorita.

00:07:48.460 --> 00:07:49.850
- You have to excuse me, please.

00:07:49.850 --> 00:07:51.050
I've got some things on the stove.

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:52.240
- Si, senorita.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:29.060
- You have but one oars? - Yeah.

00:08:30.060 --> 00:08:33.360
Tomorrow, Senor, in exchange for the use of the water...

00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:36.560
...I will bring to the Senorita a terrabred pony.

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:40.740
- Is it a wagon? - You're welcome to the water.

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:44.800
- Suit yourself about the horse. - It will be here tomorrow.

00:08:45.810 --> 00:08:47.060
Adios, amigo.

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:15.130
- There's plenty of water.

00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:18.010
- Also a very young and beautiful senorita.

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:20.680
- Tomorrow, we bring yours.

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:22.120
- Carry out a wheel.

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:24.320
- Yeah, what about the old man?

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:25.820
- The boys will attack the place.

00:09:25.820 --> 00:09:27.630
I will rescue the girl.

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:28.720
- And the old man?

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:30.000
- Well, it's bad.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.540
but he will be killed.

00:09:32.230 --> 00:09:33.510
Just another tragedy.

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:38.700
Just another romance in the life of Bandro Zandi.

00:09:47.970 --> 00:09:57.540
Randy!

00:09:58.790 --> 00:10:00.000
What's wrong?

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:04.800
- What happened? - They're going to take me away.

00:10:05.260 --> 00:10:08.900
- And they're planning to kill you. - Don't cry.

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:29.860
- Tell me what you heard. - He's going to get you out of here, Ruby.

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:33.160
I'll be back any time.

00:10:36.380 --> 00:10:38.520
I know just what we'll do.

00:10:48.270 --> 00:10:53.110
Maybe it's best to get some of the boys and the R's and return today.

00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:02.530
When I signal, you know what to do.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:05.920
They have smell of rats and have vamoose.

00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:03.240
Hello, Yorba.

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:04.450
Heading for town?

00:13:04.630 --> 00:13:06.690
I bring the horse, but I find you gone.

00:13:07.150 --> 00:13:07.940
Ruby there?

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:09.200
I have seen no one.

00:13:09.650 --> 00:13:11.410
Shucks, she must have been up to the spring.

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:14.890
See, I got to go to town for provisions and had to leave her behind.

00:13:15.390 --> 00:13:16.170
Why, no.

00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:19.180
You will perhaps bring me some bacon and flour, no?

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:20.610
I would pay you well.

00:13:21.010 --> 00:13:23.220
Give me your horse and I'll load him down for you.

00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:27.230
And in return for this, I will take good care of your granddaughter.

00:13:28.530 --> 00:13:30.000
Well, I certainly appreciate it.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:32.020
- I appreciate your kindness. - My brother?

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:38.450
- Yours. - So long. See you later.

00:13:38.520 --> 00:13:48.510
The old fool. We will not only get his provisions, but ours as well.

00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:52.530
Come. I'll carry away my new romance.

00:14:04.410 --> 00:14:06.610
They'll be watching us, Ruby. We have to keep going.

00:14:06.830 --> 00:14:08.750
Okay, Pop. I'm all right.

00:14:09.330 --> 00:14:10.650
We have to cross the river.

00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:13.060
Go ahead. I'll get out of this trouble.

00:14:53.230 --> 00:14:54.420
Give me the glass, Joe.

00:15:36.680 --> 00:15:39.510
There's a girl in the pack and I can't swim.

00:16:31.530 --> 00:16:33.720
The girl, she was in the pack.

00:17:09.150 --> 00:17:12.970
Son, them's renegades after my girl.

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:17.350
Sure appreciate your help.

00:17:17.910 --> 00:17:18.830
Certainly, old-timer.

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:20.210
It's only three miles to town.

00:17:20.920 --> 00:17:21.340
Come on.

00:20:43.180 --> 00:20:46.200
Well, I guess we're safe, Ruby, thanks to the stranger.

00:20:47.280 --> 00:20:49.880
- I suppose he's all right. - Well, I sure hope so.

00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:53.020
He'll be coming for his horse soon, I reckon.

00:20:53.340 --> 00:20:55.480
- Dumb animal. - Looks like a thoroughbred.

00:20:55.730 --> 00:21:00.000
- He is a thoroughbred man. - Well, stranger.

00:21:00.890 --> 00:21:03.330
Yes, Ruby and me, just about owe your wives.

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:06.680
Oh, you don't owe me anything, but tell me, what was it all about?

00:21:06.690 --> 00:21:10.840
Well, sir, this morning, a stranger rode up to the house and...

00:21:10.880 --> 00:21:28.000
he says to me, he says, "The stranger put it in and it got away."

00:21:28.110 --> 00:21:30.000
Right back and get the rest of the boys.

00:21:31.120 --> 00:21:33.880
We have very important business in town, too.

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:37.040
Sure enough, they trailed us.

00:21:37.900 --> 00:21:39.860
Convinced them that I'd left Ruby behind.

00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:42.420
Everything was all right till we crossed the river.

00:21:42.580 --> 00:21:44.500
What was this stranger's name?

00:21:44.710 --> 00:21:47.280
He called himself "Panbrough Zanty."

00:21:48.050 --> 00:21:49.780
- Zanty? - Yeah.

00:21:49.980 --> 00:21:51.320
I'd only known.

00:21:51.630 --> 00:21:56.980
I'd like to meet him face to face.

00:21:57.730 --> 00:22:00.000
I can fix that up for you.

00:22:00.860 --> 00:22:04.400
If I turn for your kindness today, I'll take you right where you can find it.

00:22:05.050 --> 00:22:07.190
See, I got a cabin down on the edge of the town.

00:22:07.440 --> 00:22:08.280
You can put up there.

00:22:08.750 --> 00:22:10.010
Besides, I want you to meet the sheriff.

00:22:30.060 --> 00:22:33.060
Manzante is the worst outlaw the state has ever known.

00:22:33.140 --> 00:22:35.950
Half white, half Apache Indian.

00:22:36.050 --> 00:22:40.020
He poses as a Mexican, speaks the language.

00:22:40.080 --> 00:22:46.680
- But he's not a Mexican. - Tell him about deserted.

00:22:46.730 --> 00:22:49.710
Bueno, go ahead. I will be waiting.

00:22:49.810 --> 00:23:00.000
I think the best plan is to...

00:23:00.160 --> 00:23:04.810
Eight temporary camps about 10 miles apart, along the desert.

00:23:04.900 --> 00:23:07.470
We're sure to spot him sooner or later.

00:23:07.570 --> 00:23:11.750
John Tobin here and me here are heading out that way in the morning.

00:23:11.850 --> 00:23:14.680
Well, $5,000 is worth going after.

00:23:14.720 --> 00:23:20.610
Hey, everybody, stop. Don't open that door.

00:23:20.710 --> 00:23:22.180
I'm giving orders here.

00:23:51.020 --> 00:24:00.000
It's you, eh? What have you got here?

00:24:00.280 --> 00:24:03.320
- How did he get it? - What difference does it make, as long as I've got it?

00:24:03.400 --> 00:24:06.480
It might make a lot of difference. I'll take charge of this.

00:24:06.560 --> 00:24:17.740
- Nice, agreeable and appreciative sheriff you've got here. - Yeah.

00:24:17.820 --> 00:24:21.270
He started off all right, but he's sure going to see it.

00:24:21.350 --> 00:24:25.910
Now, boys, I'm suspicious of this open.

00:24:25.990 --> 00:24:30.000
How'd he know it was Sandy? And how come he got it?

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:31.510
to get this money without getting shot.

00:24:32.390 --> 00:24:34.320
I'm going to keep an eye on him.

00:24:34.740 --> 00:24:37.360
He and old Dusty are heading for the desert in the morning.

00:24:37.460 --> 00:24:39.670
I'm going to take a couple of boys and follow him.

00:24:39.810 --> 00:24:41.560
He might lead us right to Zandie.

00:24:41.770 --> 00:24:44.600
I tell you, I don't trust nobody.

00:24:44.900 --> 00:24:48.840
Well, here it is, son.

00:24:48.880 --> 00:24:50.390
Pretty comfortable, too.

00:24:50.420 --> 00:24:51.170
Come here.

00:24:51.190 --> 00:24:56.600
Wow.

00:24:56.660 --> 00:24:58.260
Old mine tunnel.

00:24:58.340 --> 00:25:00.000
It leads the trail up above.

00:25:00.640 --> 00:25:03.240
It's coming mighty handy sometimes. It's a trouble.

00:25:38.320 --> 00:25:42.010
Hey, Dusty, you've got plenty of water.

00:25:42.010 --> 00:25:48.780
This being government ground, I reckon I'll stay right here.

00:25:48.780 --> 00:25:54.340
What a pleasant place this is, Governor.

00:25:54.340 --> 00:25:58.140
Well, Frank Tobin's been gone five days now.

00:25:58.140 --> 00:25:59.190
I wonder where he's eating.

00:25:59.190 --> 00:26:00.000
Juggie, grab with him.

00:26:00.480 --> 00:26:04.290
Yeah, it's funny him coming out of here without us knowing about it.

00:26:04.490 --> 00:26:07.290
- Didn't leave no trail either. - He likes to work alone.

00:26:07.580 --> 00:26:08.750
That's his excuse.

00:26:09.270 --> 00:26:11.270
Dusty, you ain't smart.

00:26:11.950 --> 00:26:15.780
Now, if I'm going to trail him, he'll let me ride to Zanty.

00:30:36.810 --> 00:30:40.430
You better take charge of him, Sheriff, before I cheat the law.

00:30:40.940 --> 00:30:42.580
I finally captured you, eh?

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:08.940
- This is my business. I haven't lost a prisoner yet. - You've never had one to lose.

00:31:08.940 --> 00:31:15.600
- The boys will be back tomorrow. - We'll be taking you to town.

00:31:15.600 --> 00:31:23.050
- You've been a big wolf, but I've finally got you. - You forget, Sheriff.

00:31:23.050 --> 00:31:28.740
Wolves run in packs, and mine is not far behind.

00:31:31.310 --> 00:31:36.520
I've got to go, Dusty, because I've got a growing desire to go there and break him to pieces.

00:31:36.520 --> 00:31:40.740
It's just how you feel, son. Tell Ruby I'll be home in a couple of days.

00:31:40.740 --> 00:31:42.130
All right, old-timer.

00:32:28.440 --> 00:32:29.190
Dusty.

00:32:31.720 --> 00:32:40.280
- Drop that gun, Colvin. - Don't be a fool, Sheriff.

00:32:40.590 --> 00:32:42.790
- The man who did this is getting away. - Yeah?

00:32:43.250 --> 00:32:44.930
The man who did this is right in front of me.

00:32:45.440 --> 00:32:47.120
I had you figured out right along.

00:32:48.910 --> 00:32:52.070
- Got him in the head, eh? - What's this?

00:32:57.170 --> 00:32:58.770
I suppose you're denying that's yours.

00:33:05.120 --> 00:33:05.920
Get your hands out there.

00:33:43.660 --> 00:33:44.980
Two of a kind, eh?

00:33:46.300 --> 00:33:47.760
Hold up, Sandy.

00:33:48.420 --> 00:33:51.550
This guy double-crossed you and brought you in here just to get the reward.

00:33:51.700 --> 00:33:54.000
Ain't that it?

00:33:54.100 --> 00:33:57.270
You're very wise, Senor Sheriff.

00:33:57.900 --> 00:33:58.930
Sure I am.

00:34:05.820 --> 00:34:07.910
Hello, boys. I'm glad you got here.

00:34:08.220 --> 00:34:10.980
Miller, go to town and tell the boys I got Zanty.

00:34:11.360 --> 00:34:14.080
And that ain't old. Tobin killed old Dusty.

00:34:14.850 --> 00:34:16.160
Bring all the boys you can get.

00:34:16.530 --> 00:34:18.570
We might bump into Zanty's gag on the way to town.

00:34:18.860 --> 00:34:19.780
Okay, Sheriff.

00:34:20.080 --> 00:34:22.260
Hank, stay here and keep an eye on them.

00:34:22.460 --> 00:34:24.100
I'm going to eat your friends and get Slim.

00:36:13.850 --> 00:36:14.790
Look out, Hank!

00:36:33.900 --> 00:36:39.380
- That's how you got away to kill Dusty. - Your deductions are much better than the sheriff's.

00:36:40.560 --> 00:36:45.070
I knew you did it all right. You're the only one that could have taken my knife.

00:36:45.390 --> 00:36:51.540
- What did you come back for? - To wait for this opportunity.

00:36:51.780 --> 00:36:56.120
Soon you will be with your friends and there will be only two left.

00:36:56.220 --> 00:36:59.860
The senior sheriff and his man will return from Indian Springs.

00:37:00.280 --> 00:37:04.800
I will be in ambush, then Xanti will go free.

00:37:11.500 --> 00:37:13.960
- Senor! - Pleasant dreams!

00:37:36.200 --> 00:37:38.390
Yes! Two horses ready.

00:37:39.090 --> 00:37:40.850
Easy now, son.

00:41:42.280 --> 00:41:45.300
Drink your pills, Zanty, poison.

00:42:31.310 --> 00:42:33.560
If I go without them, my reputation is ruined.

00:42:36.190 --> 00:42:38.580
And they're holding them a prisoner over to your old place.

00:42:39.130 --> 00:42:40.690
But I just can't believe he did it.

00:42:40.850 --> 00:42:42.290
Sheriff caught them right in the act.

00:42:43.020 --> 00:42:44.280
You're sorry, Miss Ruby.

00:43:07.640 --> 00:43:13.480
It's strange how they broke out of here, I know.

00:43:14.860 --> 00:43:18.020
Zandi got out, broke the chain that held Tobin,

00:43:18.690 --> 00:43:20.320
overpowered Hank and then shot him.

00:43:21.190 --> 00:43:23.170
I always knew them two were in cahoots.

00:43:43.020 --> 00:43:44.600
It's the girl. Why not stop her?

00:43:45.140 --> 00:43:47.340
They're holding Pandro. We'll make him exchange prisoners.

00:44:16.220 --> 00:44:18.940
- I need someone to take care of you.

00:44:18.940 --> 00:44:20.580
- Seems to me you're doing very well.

00:44:50.760 --> 00:44:53.040
We've got to race for them.

00:45:01.180 --> 00:45:03.780
The girl in the Umbra that got Pandra just ahead of us.

00:46:44.300 --> 00:46:45.650
Come on, boys. We got them trapped.

00:47:38.570 --> 00:47:40.870
Just a minute there, Sheriff.

00:47:41.680 --> 00:47:53.300
Faint, you old fool, I ain't dead yet.

00:47:53.400 --> 00:47:55.380
Put that shot in the knife.

00:47:55.480 --> 00:47:57.030
Oh, shucks, I want shot.

00:47:57.130 --> 00:48:00.000
For the knife is only for me.

00:48:00.000 --> 00:48:03.360
It's only a scratch. The guy who has done it is inside.

00:48:03.720 --> 00:48:16.030
- Come on. - Who's there?

00:48:16.270 --> 00:48:18.080
That's a dead man called Zanty.

00:48:18.390 --> 00:48:21.700
- He's the guy that knifed me. - What's that?

00:48:22.550 --> 00:48:23.880
That's Zanty's game.

00:48:25.150 --> 00:48:28.040
Go ahead and let him out, Sheriff. We'll help you.

00:48:38.320 --> 00:48:39.920
Just as well know I got you.

00:48:39.920 --> 00:48:42.160
Come on out one at a time.

00:48:42.160 --> 00:48:45.080
Your guns in your horses and your hands reaching high.

00:48:45.080 --> 00:48:53.020
Stand up again that wall.

00:48:53.020 --> 00:48:54.770
- Bessie, keep them covered. - You bet.

00:48:54.770 --> 00:49:00.000
Get over there.

00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:18.720
- Get over. - There's dinner tonight.
